  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Online Security Training for Partners in Bolivia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The closing of space for actors in Bolivian civil society that are critical of government policies and actions is well-documented. A number of CAFOD partners (and CAFOD in Bolivia) work on issues (such as the protection of natural resources and indigenous rights) that certain sectors of the Bolivian state seek to repress. In Bolivia, human rights defenders are not usually at risk of physical violence, a number of minor incidents have occurred that have lead several partners to suspect that their communications are under surveillance. The visit of an online security expert provides an opportunity for CAFOD and three partners (Caritas, UNITAS and the Bolivian Climate Change Platform) to analyse their security situation from all angles and learn some basic techniques and skills to achieve an improved level of online security.</narrative>
  </description>
